From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 15:24:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: vop2: recognize packed YUYV 10-bit output

The DisplayPort bridge selects MEDIA_BUS_FMT_YUYV10_1X20 when an HBR3x4
link carries 4K120 as YCbCr 4:2:2 10-bit.  Without this format in
is_yuv_output(), VOP2 does not enable its RGB-to-YUV conversion and the
sink interprets packed RGB values as YCbCr, producing severe green and
magenta color corruption.

Handle the 10-bit format in the same way as YUYV8_1X16.  This also matches
the Rockchip BSP VOP2 implementation.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
@@ -349,6 +349,7 @@ static bool is_yuv_output(u32 bus_format)
 	switch (bus_format) {
 	case MEDIA_BUS_FMT_YUV8_1X24:
 	case MEDIA_BUS_FMT_YUV10_1X30:
+	case MEDIA_BUS_FMT_YUYV10_1X20:
 	case MEDIA_BUS_FMT_UYYVYY8_0_5X24:
 	case MEDIA_BUS_FMT_UYYVYY10_0_5X30:
 	case MEDIA_BUS_FMT_YUYV8_2X8:
